---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { business, mailHref, telHref } from "../lib/site";
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${business.name} collects and uses information from this website.`} path="/privacy/">
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you book or request a quote, we collect what you give us: your name, phone number, email, the job address, a description of the job, and any photos you upload. We use it to schedule, price and do the job, and to contact you about it.</p>
  <h2>Where it goes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Our scheduling calendar</b> (Google Calendar) holds your appointment details so our crew knows where to go.</li>
    <li><b>Our hosting provider</b> stores booking records and photos.</li>
    <li><b>Email/SMS providers</b> deliver confirmations and updates, if those are turned on.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell your information, and we don't add you to marketing lists.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which parts of the site work, like how many people start a booking. It sets cookies and Google receives basic information about your visit, such as pages viewed and your general area. We don't send your name, phone, email, address or booking links to Google Analytics. You can opt out with <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google's opt-out add-on</a> or by blocking cookies in your browser.</p>
  <h2>Saved progress</h2>
  <p>The booking form saves your progress in your own browser (local storage) so you don't lose it if you leave the page. It's cleared when your booking goes through.</p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>To see, correct or delete information we hold about you, email <a href={mailHref}>{business.email}</a> or call <a href={telHref}>{business.phoneDisplay}</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
